<request-parameters>
<!--
  D176 = "Provisional Mortality Statistics, 2018 through Last Month".
  Updated monthly. Lights up Causes of Death for 2021+ (D76 stops at 2020).

  DRAFT v2. Modeled directly on the WORKING mortality_icd10.xml (D76)
  request shape, with D176 ids and D176's extra residence/occurrence
  location filters (V77/V79/V80/V100 exist only in the expanded vintage).
  All multiple-cause-of-death (MCD) machinery from D176's default envelope
  is deliberately stripped — we do underlying-cause-of-death only, exactly
  like D76. (v1 kept O_mcd + the V13/V15/V16 AND-combination boxes and
  WONDER 500'd: "The second box of the AND combination for 'MCD - ICD-10
  Codes' contains an entry while the first one is empty.")

  Still UNVERIFIED: that D176's "ICD-10 113 Cause List" is variable V4.
  It is on D76, and D176's other core variables line up with D76's
  numbering (V5=age, V9=location, V19=urbanization, V42=race), so V4 is a
  well-founded guess — but confirm with:
    cd pipeline
    node --env-file=.env fetch.js --type=mortality --era=provisional \
         --years=2021 --out=rows.json --dump
  Expect ~130 cause rows for 2021, each with death_count / population /
  crude_rate / age_adjusted_rate. If instead you get thousands of rows
  (full ICD-10 code detail) or zero, V4 is wrong — paste the <message>
  from mortality_provisional.raw.xml (or D176's variable list) and we
  re-point B_2 / O_ucd.
-->
